  "patterns": "There is no single feeder. Most non-celebrity MW guests arrive on a book cycle and do a burst of interviews on large general-interest shows (DOAC, Jordan Harbinger, Mel Robbins, Plain English, Rich Roll) in the weeks or months before MW, which points to publicist-driven tours. Modern Wisdom also recycles its own guests heavily (Joe Hudson, George Mack, Anomaly, Harrington, Freya India), and many guests or feeder hosts are podcasters themselves (Codie Sanchez, Connor Beaton, Donald Robertson, Spencer Greenberg, Johnny Chang, James Smith, Steven Bartlett, Konstantin Kisin, Mel Robbins). Peer-to-peer creator networking is therefore a major route. Viral YouTube origin stories (Johnny Chang via Soft White Underbelly, Pantano's Pursuit of Wonder) are a second route, and health founders reach MW through the JRE and Ben Greenfield circuit. No booking agency or network showed up repeatedly apart from Flightstory (DOAC); not verified.",
  "avery_path": "Avery needs a thesis-led hook that fits MW's psychology, status and success lens. A good candidate is 'the psychology of status, taste and money in the blue-chip art world' (how hype is manufactured, why billionaires buy art), not just a founder biography. Step 1: land 4-6 mid-tier entrepreneur and lifestyle shows where his story fits naturally (School of Greatness, The Skinny Confidential Him & Her, Hot Smart Rich, and the guest's own podcasting peers) to build clips and a guest reel. Step 2: use those clips to pitch Jordan Harbinger (insider-world and persuasion angle) and Mel Robbins or Jay Shetty (purpose and philanthropy angle), the shows that precede MW most often in this sample. Step 3: get on shows whose hosts are in Chris Williamson's circle (Codie Sanchez's BigDeal, James Smith's The Problem With, DOAC) and pitch MW directly with a short clip plus a status-psychology or art-market thesis, ideally tied to a book or major news event, since that matches the timing of most MW bookings."
}